  "comment": "Measured river border-alignment baseline, produced by tools/validators/validate_adiscord_map_rivers.py on 2026-08-19. A HOI4 river only produces a river-crossing combat penalty where it lies on the border between two provinces, so border alignment is the correct target - but moving a channel onto a border CREATES a penalty that did not exist, which changes combat balance. These numbers are why no rerouting was done: the channel is already 97% border-aligned and the interior tail is 776 pixels across a handful of short systems, so a map-wide reroute would move far more combat modifiers than it fixed. The validator holds this line as a floor, so a future pass cannot silently push rivers off the borders, and worst_systems keeps the remaining tail visible.",
